  [1mDesign (short version)[0m

  - [1mZero new dependencies.[0m JWT signing/verification and password hashing use [38;5;153mnode:crypto[39m (HS256 hand-rolled over
    base64url; scrypt for passwords). This keeps the POC installable behind the proxy and avoids [38;5;153mjsonwebtoken[39m/[38;5;153mbcrypt[39m.
  - [1mMock email to stdout.[0m "Password reset" prints the reset link/token via [38;5;153mconsole.log[39m. No SMTP, no transport config.
  - [1mSmall modules[0m rather than one fat [38;5;153mapp.js[39m: [38;5;153msrc/store.js[39m (users + reset tokens), [38;5;153msrc/passwords.js[39m, [38;5;153msrc/jwt.js[39m,
    [38;5;153msrc/mailer.js[39m, [38;5;153msrc/middleware.js[39m ([38;5;153mrequireAuth[39m), [38;5;153msrc/routes/auth.js[39m. [38;5;153mapp.js[39m stays wiring only.
  - [1mEndpoints:[0m [38;5;153mPOST /auth/register[39m, [38;5;153mPOST /auth/login[39m, [38;5;153mPOST /auth/forgot-password[39m, [38;5;153mPOST /auth/reset-password[39m, and [38;5;153mGET /me
[39m    as the protected route.
  - [1mTokens:[0m HS256, 24h [38;5;153mexp[39m, secret from [38;5;153mprocess.env.JWT_SECRET[39m with a dev fallback.
  - [1mTests:[0m one [38;5;153mnode:test[39m file exercising the full flow (register → login → protected → reset). The repo has no test
    infra; this adds the minimum.

  Assumptions I'm making without asking: single-process in-memory state (restart wipes everything), no refresh tokens,
  no rate limiting, no email verification, reset tokens are single-use with a short TTL, and login/forgot responses
  don't leak whether an email exists.

  Writing the spec now.

